foundation.question_text:
A trigonometric graph is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.3, xmax=6.8, ymin=-4, ymax=4,
  xtick={1.5708, 3.1416, 4.7124, 6.2832},
  xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$, $\frac{3\pi}{2}$, $2\pi$},
  ytick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3},
  samples=200, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-4:4, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=11cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0.01:1.45] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=1.69:4.59] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=4.83:6.27] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({1.5708},{x});
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({4.7124},{x});
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Identify which trigonometric function is shown: $y = \sin x$, $y = \cos x$, or $y = \tan x$.

mastery.question_text:
The graphs of $y = \sin x$ and $y = \cos x$ are plotted together on $[0, 2\pi]$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.3, xmax=6.8, ymin=-1.4, ymax=1.4,
  xtick={1.5708, 3.1416, 4.7124, 6.2832},
  xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$, $\frac{3\pi}{2}$, $2\pi$},
  ytick={-1, 1},
  samples=200, clip=false,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=11cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0:6.2832] {sin(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, red, dashed, domain=0:6.2832] {cos(deg(x))};
\node[blue, above right] at (axis cs:2.6,0.5) {$y=\sin x$};
\node[red, below left] at (axis cs:2.0944,-0.5) {$y=\cos x$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Find all values of $x$ in $[0, 2\pi]$ where $\sin x = \cos x$, and state the coordinates of the intersection points.
